between its demanding tactical battles  deep class system and social some  elements fireman three houses can seem a  bit overwhelming if you don't know what  you're doing you and your students could  be at a significant disadvantage here's  some tips that could give you an edge in  Fire Emblem three houses after you pick  your house black eagles for life you'll  be assigned to a group of students but  eventually you'll be able to recruit  students from other houses in order to  recruit someone you'll need to talk to  them and complete a basic skill check if  your bond and skills are high enough  they will agree to join your class I'd  recommend recruiting all the characters  you like as soon as possible because  there's no telling where they might end  up later in the game terrain conditions  can make a huge difference in fire  emblem trees make your ground units  harder to hit but decrease their  movement range standing in fire will  naturally harm characters over time and  sand makes it really hard for your  mounted units to move but there are ways  to use terrain to your advantage some  classes like the bishop are immune to  fire for example while mounted units can  temporarily dismount to better Traverse  and  these items will give you a brief  description of who they belong to and  you must return them when you return a  lost item to a student or faculty member  your bond with that character will  increase and if they're in your class  they will gain a bit of motivation lost  items typically appear where someone was  hanging out the month before so if you  get stuck on one think back to who might  have been in the area if you find a lost  item for someone who already has max  motivation I would consider waiting to  return it until after their motivation  drops  it can be tough building up violets  skills since you can't directly teach  them like you can with your students if  you do need to level up a certain scale  professors scattered around the  monastery can give by lift one-on-one  lessons however I wouldn't worry too  much about baile skills when it comes to  which class you should aim for without  spoiling too much things will fall into  place eventually support levels and  conversations are back and they function  pretty similarly to before as you battle  and bond with your students you will  unlock conversations that rank up  support levels not only will you learn  more about your students but you'll get  a stat bonus when two or more friends  are near each other on the battlefield  so make sure to check the support menu  often  don't forget to manage your units  abilities before battle as a character  levels up in different skills they  unlock abilities that correspond to what  they've learned like better stats when  wielding an axe or higher avoidance when  using magic the abilities have to be  manually equipped so make sure you've  slaughtered in abilities that match the  unit's current class and load out before  you start fighting probably one of the  most important battle tips in this video  is to use Zr to see the range of your  enemies when you press the R you will  see purple outlines around tiles if a  unit is inside one of those purple tiles  that means the enemy is within reach of  your unit you might even want to leave  this on throughout the entire battle  especially if there are Pegasus and  wyvern units on the battlefield  [Music]  if you aren't sure how to spend your  time during a free day in game I  recommend sharing a meal or two with  your students this is a good way to bond  with them increase their motivation and  build up your professor level eventually  you'll unlock a blacksmith in the  marketplace  here you can strengthen and repair your  weapons keep in mind that repairing  weapons will cost you gold and smithing  stones  I wouldn't recommend repairing every  weapon as it can eat through a lot of  resources in gold but there are some  weapons you get later that are worth  repairing  you can also Forge rusted weapons you  find on the battlefield into useable  weapons with some goal and materials  fire inland three houses is a complex  game especially if you're unfamiliar  with the series but once you get the  hang of it it's a deeply satisfying  tactical RPG hopefully these tips helped  and if you have any other tips please  leave them in the comments below thank  you so much for watching  [Music]
 

